  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large clay pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic, ginger, cumin, coriander, cayenne pepper, turmeric, and paprika. Cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the chicken and cook until browned on all sides, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the salt, black pepper, cilantro, parsley, lemon juice, chicken broth, and water. Stir to combine.",
    "Bring the mixture to a boil, then cover the pot and transfer it to the oven.",
    "Bake at 375°F for 30 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and the broth is rich and flavorful.",
    "If using harissa, stir it in before serving.",
    "Serve the chicken and broth hot, garnished with additional cilantro and parsley if desired.",
    "Garnish with toasted almonds or pine nuts, if desired."
  ],
